.SH NAME
writ\-export \- print the log and valid statements of an identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nh
.ad l
\fBwrit export\fR \fB\-i\fR\ \fIDIR\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR]
.ad
.hy
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a bundle with the log of the identity in DIR and every statement it issued that is valid now, including revocations. Give this bundle to the people who check your statements.
.PP
Data signatures are left out, because they travel with the data they sign.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-identity\fR \fIDIR\fR
the identity to export
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
also print expired and revoked statements, and data signatures
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print help; \fB\-h\fR is short, \fB\-\-help\fR is long
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
success; for questions, the answer is yes
.TP
1
the answer is no: the check, verification, proof or name lookup was denied
.TP
2
an error: bad usage, unreadable input, or a failed operation
.SH EXAMPLES
Publish your statements:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
writ export \-i me > me.writ
.fi
.RE
